---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Introduction">
  <article class="docs">
    <h1>FunctionFly™ Documentation</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      Welcome to FunctionFly™, the fastest way to deploy serverless functions to the global edge.
      This guide will help you get started with deploying your code to 35+ edge locations worldwide.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Quick Start</h2>
      <p>Get up and running in less than 2 minutes:</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <pre><code><span class="code-comment"># Install the fly CLI (Go 1.25+)</span>
<span class="code-prompt">$</span> go install github.com/functionfly/functionfly/cmd/fly@latest

<span class="code-comment"># Or download from https://github.com/functionfly/functionfly/releases</span>

<span class="code-comment"># Login to FunctionFly™</span>
<span class="code-prompt">$</span> fly login

<span class="code-comment"># Initialize a new function</span>
<span class="code-prompt">$</span> fly init my-function

<span class="code-comment"># Deploy to the edge</span>
<span class="code-prompt">$</span> fly deploy</code></pre>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What is FunctionFly™?</h2>
      <p>
        FunctionFly™ is a serverless platform that lets you deploy functions to edge locations
        around the world. Your code runs closer to your users, resulting in lower latency
        and better user experience.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>35+ Edge Locations</strong> - Deploy to major cities across North America, Europe, Asia, and Australia</li>
        <li><strong>Multi-runtime Support</strong> - Write functions in JavaScript, TypeScript, Python, or Go</li>
        <li><strong>Enterprise Security</strong> - Built-in malware scanning, signature verification, and trust levels</li>
        <li><strong>Real-time Analytics</strong> - Monitor function performance with detailed metrics</li>
        <li><strong>Easy Integrations</strong> - Connect to GitHub, Slack, Stripe, and 100+ other services</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Key Concepts</h2>

      <h3 id="functions">Functions</h3>
      <p>
        A function is a single unit of code that can be executed in response to events.
        Functions can be written in any supported runtime and are deployed to edge locations.
      </p>

      <h3 id="deployments">Deployments</h3>
      <p>
        A deployment is the process of publishing your function to the edge. Each deployment
        creates a new version that can be rolled back if needed.
      </p>

      <h3 id="edges">Edge Locations</h3>
      <p>
        Edge locations are data centers distributed around the world. When you deploy a function,
        it automatically replicates to all edge locations, ensuring fast access from anywhere.
      </p>

      <h3 id="trust-levels">Trust Levels</h3>
      <p>
        Trust levels determine how verified and safe your functions are. Higher trust levels
        require more rigorous verification but provide better performance and reliability.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Next Steps</h2>
      <p>Ready to dive in? Here are some helpful resources:</p>

      <div class="resource-grid">
        <a href="/docs/quick-start" class="resource-card">
          <h4>Quick Start Guide</h4>
          <p>Learn the basics in 5 minutes</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/cli" class="resource-card">
          <h4>CLI Reference</h4>
          <p>Complete command reference</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/api" class="resource-card">
          <h4>API Reference</h4>
          <p>Programmatic access documentation</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/docs/examples" class="resource-card">
          <h4>Examples</h4>
          <p>Real-world function examples</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .docs {
    max-width: 800px;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
  }

  p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }

  li {
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  li::before {
    content: "→";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  li strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .code-block {
    background: #1a1f2e;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .code-block pre {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .code-block code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .code-comment {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .code-prompt {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .resource-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .resource-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-light);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .resource-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-primary);
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .resource-card h4 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .resource-card p {
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .resource-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
